From: Project Management <project@bluewater-energy.example> (Bluewater Energy Services)
To: Project Management <project@mercon-steel.example> (Mercon Steel Structures)
Date: 2008-11-11
Subject: Notice of Partial Termination of the Work - Central Column coating

Further to our Notice of Default of 31 October 2008: after transport of the Central Column to the ASPO yard "it was noticed that the special abrasive coating (Inerta) was damaged and adhesions failures were observed between the two coats". BLUEWATER notified MERCON that the coating used was rejected. MERCON has said that it will not remedy the coating unless BLUEWATER accepts liability for the defects.

As MERCON has failed to remedy the default, BLUEWATER hereby gives notice of partial termination of the Work, removing the coating repair of the Central Column from MERCON's scope.

--
RECONSTRUCTED FROM THE PUBLISHED JUDGMENT. Not an original document.
Source: Bluewater v Mercon [2014] EWHC 2132 (TCC), paras 11, 76, 199, 1370-1371.
Wording of both notices not quoted in the source; senders, addresses and signatories not stated.
